==============================================================================
Synthesis
==============================================================================
Even numbers/graphs are kernel objects: boundary zero.  Odd line
graphs are affine boundary objects: boundary one on the SC support.
So the useful identity is not just 'tournaments are equinumerous with
even graphs'; it is 'the black complement-line lift is already an
even graph, while the blue lift is the odd coset whose boundary tells
which SC nodes kept a grid-symmetric witness.'
